 s\, fjs)\;})(window\, document\, 'script'\, 'qgiv-embedjs')\; Have you eve
 r been interested in joining Cool Petaluma's block-based Cool Teams progra
 m but faced barriers to implementing it in your neighborhood?&nbsp\; Thank
 s to the support of our two AmeriCorps fellows\, Auggie and Raelyn\, Cool 
 Petaluma will be offering a monthly Cool Teams program open to anyone inte
 rested in turning climate concern into collective action! Beginning on Mar
 ch 25th\, sessions will be held from 6 pm to 7:30 pm on the last Wednesday
  of each month. May’s session: Topic: Rethink Consumption: From food to 
 fashion\, we can reimagine the full lifecycle of our stuff\, eliminating w
 aste and pollution while increasing longevity and sharing. We’ll cover h
 ow to eat wisely\, shop smart and share more\, and vote with your dollar. 
 Bring your own consumption hack ideas to share!&nbsp\; Location: Held at t
 he brand new Porches office at 11 5th St (at B st) For some entertaining a
 nd educational "Rethink Consumption" themed videos to&nbsp\;get you thinki
 ng about our next topic\, check out the Cool Petaluma YouTube playlist her
 e . (John Oliver’s Food Waste rant is a great one.) If you've been unabl
 e to implement our program in the past due to HOA&nbsp\;restrictions\, dif
 ficult neighborhood locations\, lack of time\, or the demands of leadershi
 p\, now is your chance to participate. Don't miss out on this special oppo
 rtunity to connect with like-minded neighbors! #block-902c9aab7f69c1e4c67f
